      "chat_binding": {
        "chat_id": "chat-0192ab",
        "origin_message_id": "msg-0004",
        "bound_at": "2026-09-08T09:12:44Z"
      },
      "question": "Should the workshop take the recurring 40-unit order at 0.7x price?",
      "context_snapshot": {
        "content_type": "text/plain",
        "byte_length": 210,
        "content_hash": "sha256:245476750cd4f559065eab75c62e85e2fc50ea1fef95ba1417dd3ee838db844d",
        "inline": "Order under consideration: 40 units a month for a year, at 0.7x the current unit price. Observed: the bench cleared 52 units last month with two late evenings, and 31 units in the week the jig was being re-set."
      },
      "status": "complete",
      "runs": [
        {
          "run_id": "run-1",
          "request_id": "req-round-1",
          "kind": "initial_round",
          "status": "partial",
          "started_at": "2026-09-08T09:12:45Z",
          "ended_at": "2026-09-08T09:14:45Z",
          "contributions": [
            {
              "contribution_id": "con-1",
              "seat_id": "seat-costing",
              "member_id": "mem-costing",
              "member_revision": 1,
              "status": "complete",
              "model_id": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
              "text": "At 0.7x the order pays for 28 units of revenue while consuming 40 units of bench time, so it is only worth taking if the freed capacity has no better use.",
              "claims": [
                {
                  "claim_id": "clm-1",
                  "support": "inference",
                  "text": "Forty units at 0.7x earns what twenty-eight units earn at full price, so the order costs twelve units of margin a month before anything else is counted.",
                  "citations": []
                },
                {
                  "claim_id": "clm-2",
                  "support": "inference",
                  "text": "A year of it removes 480 units of bench time from everything else the shop might take.",
                  "citations": []
                },
                {
                  "claim_id": "clm-3",
                  "support": "unknown",
                  "text": "Whether the shop has better uses for those hours is not in the material given to me.",
                  "citations": []
                }
              ],
              "usage": {
                "prompt_tokens": 1180,
                "completion_tokens": 210
              }
            },
            {
              "contribution_id": "con-2",
              "seat_id": "seat-capacity",
              "member_id": "mem-okonkwo",
              "member_revision": 3,
              "status": "failed",
              "claims": [],
              "failure": {
                "code": "timeout",
                "message": "seat-capacity did not answer inside this council's time limit.",
                "retryable": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "synthesis": {
            "contribution_id": "con-3",
            "seat_id": "seat-chair",
            "member_id": "mem-chair",
            "member_revision": 1,
            "status": "complete",
            "model_id": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
            "text": "One member answered. On the numbers alone the order costs twelve units of margin a month and 480 units of bench time over the year, and whether that is worth paying depends on what else those hours could have done \u2014 which nobody in this round could say.",
            "claims": [
              {
                "claim_id": "clm-4",
                "support": "inference",
                "text": "Unit costing's position is that the order is only worth taking if the capacity it consumes has no better use.",
                "citations": []
              },
              {
                "claim_id": "clm-5",
                "support": "unknown",
                "text": "This round is partial: 1 of 2 consulted members did not answer, so anything they would have contributed is not established here. seat-capacity: seat-capacity did not answer inside this council's time limit.",
                "citations": []
              }
            ],
            "usage": {
              "prompt_tokens": 2140,
              "completion_tokens": 260
            }
          },
          "failure": {
            "code": "timeout",
            "message": "The round was synthesised without every member. seat-capacity: seat-capacity did not answer inside this council's time limit.",
            "retryable": true
          }
        },
        {
          "run_id": "run-2",
          "request_id": "req-round-1-retry",
          "kind": "retry",
          "status": "complete",
          "started_at": "2026-09-08T09:16:02Z",
          "ended_at": "2026-09-08T09:16:58Z",
          "contributions": [
            {
              "contribution_id": "con-4",
              "seat_id": "seat-capacity",
              "member_id": "mem-okonkwo",
              "member_revision": 3,
              "status": "complete",
              "model_id": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
              "text": "Price the order against the worst week, not the average one, and price it as the sale of your right to refuse the next job.",
              "claims": [
                {
                  "claim_id": "clm-6",
                  "support": "source",
                  "text": "A recurring order is not additional work; it removes the freedom to decline, and that is what is being sold.",
                  "citations": [
                    {
                      "source_id": "src-capacity-essay",
                      "source_revision": 2,
                      "anchor_id": "anc-freedom"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "claim_id": "clm-7",
                  "support": "source",
                  "text": "Capacity is what the hard week clears, not what the easy week clears, so a quote built on the month's total is built on a bench the shop does not have.",
                  "citations": [
                    {
                      "source_id": "src-capacity-letter",
                      "source_revision": 1,
                      "anchor_id": "anc-hard-week"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "claim_id": "clm-8",
                  "support": "inference",
                  "text": "The observed 31-unit week is the number this order should be quoted against, which puts 40 units a month above the shop's real capacity.",
                  "citations": []
                },
                {
                  "claim_id": "clm-9",
                  "support": "unknown",
                  "text": "Nothing in the captured writing says what a fair premium for that lost freedom would be.",
                  "citations": []
                }
              ],
              "usage": {
                "prompt_tokens": 2260,
                "completion_tokens": 320
              }
            }
          ],
          "synthesis": {
            "contribution_id": "con-5",
            "seat_id": "seat-chair",
            "member_id": "mem-chair",
            "member_revision": 1,
            "status": "complete",
            "model_id": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
            "text": "The retried seat answers that the order should be quoted against the shop's worst week \u2014 31 units \u2014 and priced as the sale of the right to refuse work, which puts 40 units a month above real capacity. This does not agree with the earlier costing answer, which treated the month's total as the capacity and made the decision turn only on margin; the disagreement is about which number describes the bench, and it is not resolved here.",
            "claims": [
              {
                "claim_id": "clm-10",
                "support": "source",
                "text": "The capacity member's position rests on the captured claim that a recurring order removes the freedom to decline.",
                "citations": [
                  {
                    "source_id": "src-capacity-essay",
                    "source_revision": 2,
                    "anchor_id": "anc-freedom"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "claim_id": "clm-11",
                "support": "inference",
                "text": "The two members disagree about what the bench's capacity is: the month's total, or the worst week inside it.",
                "citations": []
              },
              {
                "claim_id": "clm-12",
                "support": "unknown",
                "text": "What premium would compensate for the lost freedom is established by nothing either member was given.",
                "citations": []
              }
            ],
            "usage": {
              "prompt_tokens": 2480,
              "completion_tokens": 300
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "outcomes": [
        {
          "outcome_id": "out-1",
          "run_id": "run-2",
          "contribution_id": "con-5",
          "note": {
            "kind": "note",
